{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are implemented via the existing `Analytics` wrapper, and the summary is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`)\n- `registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started` — fire once, the first time each field goes from empty to non-empty; the typed text is never captured (PII rule).\n- `loan_amount_changed` — fired on slider `onChangeEnd` once per drag with the final chosen value as an int.\n- `terms_accepted` — fires only when the checkbox is ticked, not unticked.\n- `registration_continue_tapped` — fired before navigation with `amount` (int) and `terms` (bool).\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`)\n- Converted from stateless to stateful to hold a `ScrollController`.\n- `offers_scrolled` — fires once per visit, the first time the list reaches a non-zero offset, with `offset` as a double.\n\nTwo judgment calls, both driven by the funnel use case and recorded in `ANSWER.md`: the \"started\"/\"scrolled\" events are one-shot per visit rather than per keystroke/frame (a raw scroll listener or `onChanged` would spam an event per frame), and \"chosen amount\" is read at the end of a drag, not on every intermediate value.\n\nOne caveat: I couldn't run `flutter analyze` to verify — the Flutter/Dart binaries on this machine exist but the sandbox refuses to execute them (\"Operation not permitted\"). The changes were reviewed manually; please run `flutter analyze` locally to confirm."}
